[NativeAOT] Read the byte-packed LSDA offsets without a misaligned load

A method's LSDA is byte-packed with no padding: a one-byte flags field
followed by 32-bit offsets. UnixNativeCodeManager and RuntimeInstance read
those offsets with *dac_cast<PTR_int32_t>(p), so the load lands on a
4-byte-aligned address only by chance. The cast also tells the compiler
that the address is aligned, which the format does not promise.

x64 and arm64 do not care. A RISC-V execution environment may support
misaligned access in hardware, emulate it, or reject it, and the runtime
cannot tell which, so it should not ask for it here. Build flags do not
help: with -mstrict-align the compiler still emits a single lw, because the
cast promised the alignment.

Read the offsets a byte at a time through NativePrimitiveDecoder, which
already reads these blobs. It gets a non-mutating PeekInt32, and
ReadInt32/ReadUInt32 now use it instead of repeating the byte assembly.
Widening each byte before the shift also removes the signed overflow the
old expressions had in the top byte.

Nothing is lost where misaligned access is available: with clang 22.1.8 at
-O2 the affected paths still compile to one ldrsw on arm64 and one movslq
on x64.
--- a/src/coreclr/nativeaot/Runtime/NativePrimitiveDecoder.h
+++ b/src/coreclr/nativeaot/Runtime/NativePrimitiveDecoder.h
@@ -46,17 +46,31 @@ public:
         return value;
     }
 
+    // The encodings read here are byte-packed, so a 32-bit field can start at any
+    // address. Assemble it out of byte loads: a wide load at a misaligned address
+    // faults on a target that does not implement misaligned access, and a compiler
+    // for a target that does implement it folds these back into one wide load.
+    static uint32_t PeekUInt32(const uint8_t* p)
+    {
+        return (uint32_t)*p | ((uint32_t)*(p+1) << 8) | ((uint32_t)*(p+2) << 16) | ((uint32_t)*(p+3) << 24);
+    }
+
+    static int32_t PeekInt32(const uint8_t* p)
+    {
+        return (int32_t)PeekUInt32(p);
+    }
+
     static int32_t ReadInt32(uint8_t* & p)
     {
-        int32_t value = *p | (*(p+1) << 8) | (*(p+2) << 16) | (*(p+3) << 24);
-        p += 4;
+        int32_t value = PeekInt32(p);
+        p += sizeof(int32_t);
         return value;
     }
 
     static uint32_t ReadUInt32(uint8_t* & p)
     {
-        uint32_t value = *p | (*(p+1) << 8) | (*(p+2) << 16) | (*(p+3) << 24);
-        p += 4;
+        uint32_t value = PeekUInt32(p);
+        p += sizeof(uint32_t);
         return value;
     }
 };
